  "findings": [
    "Nine OCR initialization requests and one Ghost request retained all ten CPU leases. Twenty-two later requests waited for CPU; memory admission was not their pending resource.",
    "Async worker onmessage handlers accessed null before their try/catch, so no RPC error was returned. The rejected callback did not settle the parent request and its scheduled CPU lease.",
    "OCR lexical inspection found module/api/admitted undefined; Ghost waiting IO maps were empty. This does not establish a TSV admission deadlock or active descriptor migration deadlock.",
    "SIFT reported a real ArrayBuffer refusal; a later worker reclassified it as MEMORY_LIMIT, losing its allocator-domain evidence. The first targeted recovery retired 3410657280 bytes of L2 backing.",
    "Unreadable transport is not by itself proof of OOM. Chromium deserialization can return null; exact allocator cause of these ten null messages is not measured."
  ],
